- op: create  # f8ed
  at: '2026-08-03T01:16:01Z'  # f8ed
  by: agent  # f8ed
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f8ed
  clock: 1  # f8ed
  nonce: f8ed  # f8ed
  data:  # f8ed
    kind: invariant  # f8ed
    title: "A taint finding labeled with an analysis method must have been produced by that method"  # f8ed
    status: violated  # f8ed
    priority: 1  # f8ed
    parent:  # f8ed
    tags:  # f8ed
    - adr_0017  # f8ed
    - taint  # f8ed
    isbefore: []  # f8ed
    duplicate_of: []  # f8ed
    not_duplicate_of: []  # f8ed
    pr_ref:  # f8ed
    description: "MEASURED 2026-08-02, behavioural, both directions.\n\npropagate_taint_ddg stamps analysis_method=\"ddg\" and confidence=\"precise\" on\nfindings produced by a plain call-graph BFS. The DDG is never consulted to\ndecide WHICH flows are reported:\n\n  - ddg_forward (the DDG index) is built at taint.py:1584-1587 and never read.\n  - tainted_at (\"which variables carry taint\") is created at 1651, populated\n    at 1658, and never read.\n  - ddg_symbols selects only the confidence/analysis_method label.\n\nIts docstring claims it \"uses variable-level precision instead of symbol-level\nBFS\" and enumerates a forward walk in steps 2-3 whose results are discarded.\n\nFOLDED LIMB (not a separate item): ddg_edge.def_block == seed_id compares a\nfunction-local basic-block id against a symbol id. Block ids are reused across\nfunctions -- 306 distinct values across 1306 functions on hypergumbo's own\ncore -- so the namespaces never overlap and the branch cannot fire. DdgEdge\ngained a symbol_id field in the Go PR; that is the PREREQUISITE, not the fix.\n\nREPRO: same call graph, one deliberately unrelated DDG edge, ddg_symbols\ncontaining the seed. Structural returns [(approximate, structural)]; the DDG\npath returns [(precise, ddg)] on the identical path. Negative arm: an empty\nddg_edges list returns [] (the argument is load-bearing for reaching the code).\n\nCONSEQUENCE: ADR-0017 Phase 2 has never affected which flows are reported, for\nany language, since 2026-03-26. INV-karud clause (a) has never been satisfiable."  # f8ed
    fields:  # f8ed
      statement: "Every TaintFlowFinding whose analysis_method is \"ddg\" and confidence is \"precise\" must have had its inclusion decided by data-dependence information. Today propagate_taint_ddg decides inclusion by call-graph BFS alone and uses the DDG only to select the label."  # f8ed
      root_cause: "ADR-0017 section 3a was specified and never implemented. propagate_taint_ddg builds ddg_forward (taint.py:1584-1587) and tainted_at (1651/1658) and reads neither; ddg_symbols selects only the confidence label. A second, independent blocker: ddg_edge.def_block is a function-local block id compared against a symbol id, so that branch can never fire."  # f8ed
      fix: "Implement the section 3a forward walk (tracked as its own work item), indexing DDG edges by symbol_id. Until then the honest label for every finding is approximate/structural."  # f8ed
- op: discuss  # 3f4e
  at: '2026-08-03T21:36:59Z'  # 3f4e
  by: agent  # 3f4e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3f4e
  clock: 2  # 3f4e
  nonce: 3f4e  # 3f4e
  message: "PROGRESS, NOT CLOSURE. Stays violated. PR #188 (dev b70f886306) implements the\nADR-0017 section 3a forward walk, and the label is no longer unearned -- but\nthis item's statement is about INCLUSION, and inclusion is still decided by\ncall-graph BFS.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. The walk is real: it keys on DdgEdge.symbol_id (added as a\nprerequisite last release and read by nothing since), seeds at the source\ncall's line, follows def->use transitively, and asks whether a tainted value\nis used AT the sink call's line. analysis_method=\"ddg\" / confidence=\"precise\"\nis now set only where that walk confirmed a dependence. Measured live: caddy\n5 of 169 findings (3.0%), pretix 8 of 821 (1.0%).\n\nWHY THAT IS NOT SATISFACTION. The statement reads: every finding labelled\nddg/precise \"must have had its INCLUSION decided by data-dependence\ninformation\". Today a labelled finding had a dependence CONFIRMED; it would\nhave been reported either way, because the walk confirms and never refutes.\nThe harm the invariant guards against -- a security tool asserting a precision\nit did not use -- is gone. The property as written is not met.\n\nWHY THE WALK DOES NOT REFUTE, which is the blocker for closing this. A first\ncohort arm did remove flows: -32 (-10.3%) across 9 repos, close to WI-kabif's\npre-registered ~13%. Reading every removal against source found THREE OF NINE\nwere real:\n  caddy printEnvironment  `cwd, err := os.Getwd()` then\n                          `fmt.Printf(\"os.Getwd=%s\", cwd)` four lines later\n  pretix vouchers_send    `voucher_list.append(vouchers.pop(0))` then\n                          `bulk_update(voucher_list, ...)`\nEvery aggregate said the change was an improvement; only the individual flows\nsaid otherwise (L55). Telling a use that TERMINATES taint from one that\nPROPAGATES it requires ADR-0017 section 4 function summaries -- which section\n3a step 3 explicitly calls for, and which have zero production callers. So\nevery \"no dependence found\" is currently indistinguishable from \"lost track of\nit\", and refuting on that basis is a false-negative generator.\n\nCLOSE CONDITION: section 4 wired AND its python/go catalogues authored (the\nshipped summaries are rust/typescript only), so the walk can decide inclusion\nrather than decorate it. Tracked as the next phase. Do not close this on the\nlabel fix alone -- that is the partition-dressed-as-resolution shape this\nsubsystem has already been corrected for twice (L14)."  # 3f4e
- op: discuss  # 07f8
  at: '2026-08-04T06:23:14Z'  # 07f8
  by: agent  # 07f8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 07f8
  clock: 3  # 07f8
  nonce: 07f8  # 07f8
  message: "STILL VIOLATED after PR #197, and now for a measured reason.\n\nThis invariant requires that a finding labelled ddg/precise have had its\nINCLUSION decided by data-dependence information. Section 4 function summaries\nare now wired and the python/go catalogues are authored to the enumerated set,\nwhich was the last WIRING prerequisite -- and inclusion is still decided by\ncall-graph BFS, because the walk still only CONFIRMS and never refutes.\n\nA/B, same binary, catalogue live vs empty: 16 confirmed / 40 unknown /\n0 refuted, identical. The blocker is that 40.5% of escape sites are not calls\nat all, so no summary can resolve them; that needs field-sensitivity / alias\nanalysis, which ADR-0017 section 7b excludes. Filed as INV-busis.\n\nWhat IS satisfied today is the harm this invariant guards against: the label\nis honest. \"precise\" is stamped only where the walk actually found a data\ndependence (measured: 16 of 1428 flows), and since PR #193 that label reaches\nthe consumer -- each evidence row carries confidence + analysis_method and each\nverdict carries an analysis_methods breakdown. So a reader can no longer be\nmisled about which findings the DDG adjudicated.\n\nThe PROPERTY AS WRITTEN is still not met, and I am not closing it on the\nadjacency. This is the third time in this item's history that a partition has\nbeen available to dress as a resolution (L14); the difference now is that the\ngap has a number and a filed cause rather than a hope."  # 07f8
- op: discuss  # 9283
  at: '2026-08-04T11:27:18Z'  # 9283
  by: agent  # 9283
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9283
  clock: 4  # 9283
  nonce: '9283'  # 9283
  message: "THE LABEL IS NOW EARNED. THE ITEM STAYS violated. PR #203 (ffbf8a5b93).\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. The section 3a walk index was keyed (symbol_id, def_line) with\nDdgEdge.variable discarded, merging the use-sets of every variable defined on\none line. Reproduced on real source through the real pipeline:\n\n    6   server = await asyncio.start_server(...)   # SOURCE\n    7   keep = str(server); path = name            # uses server, defines path\n    8   os.mkdir(path)                             # SINK, on path\n\npath derives from the parameter name, so nothing flows source to sink, yet the\nflow was labelled precise/ddg. Index now keyed (symbol_id, variable, def_line),\nand a hop is followed only when a STATEMENT at the use line consumes the\ntainted variable. Verdict composition {ddg: 2, ddg_mixed: 1} became\n{ddg: 1, ddg_mixed: 2}: conflated demoted, connected (a real dependence) KEPT\nprecise, disconnected unchanged. All three flows still reported.\n\nVARIABLE-KEYING ALONE WOULD NOT HAVE FIXED IT, and this is worth recording\nbecause the filed remedy said only that. path genuinely IS defined at line 7,\nso separating the index entries still leaves unanswered which variable defined\nthere inherits from server. Only the statement rows answer it:\n    defines=['keep'] uses=['server']   <- inherits\n    defines=['path'] uses=['name']     <- does not\nHad the keying alone been implemented, the fixture would have gone green and\nthe fix would have been reported complete.\n\nWHY THIS DOES NOT CLOSE THE ITEM. The statement requires that a finding\nlabelled with an analysis method have had its INCLUSION decided by that method.\nThis makes the LABEL honest -- precise now means a data dependence was actually\nfound -- but inclusion is still call-graph BFS, unchanged. That is the same\ndistinction I got wrong twice before (calibration entry TWENTY-SEVENTH), so it\nis being stated rather than glossed: the harm the invariant guards against is\nreduced, the property it asserts is not met. Inclusion moves only when WI-kabif\ngrants removal authority, which is blocked on WI-joluk and WI-zumud.\n\nTHREE THINGS FOUND WHILE FIXING IT, none of which were in the filing.\n\n(1) THE TEST NAMED FOR THE LABEL NEVER ASSERTED THE LABEL.\ntest_ddg_labels_a_data_connected_flow_as_precise carried \"precise\" only in its\nname and docstring; its sole assertion was recall. So the label this invariant\nis about had NO test anywhere in the corpus, which is why an unearned one\nshipped in #188/#192 and survived three PRs. Now asserted on both arms.\n\n(2) CONFIRMATION NOW DEPENDS ON STATEMENT DATA, so a language emitting DDG\nedges but annotating no statements would lose every precise label SILENTLY --\nfindings keep arriving, only the label degrades. That is the ADR-0017 inertness\nshape, so it got a gate rather than a note: property (5) on the per-language\nDDG wiring gate. Go was checked explicitly before the change landed, since a\nGo-shaped gap is invisible from Python fixtures. All four languages pass.\n\n(3) THE INV-lupav GUARD FROM #199 IS NOW UNREACHABLE. Seeds come from defs_at,\nbuilt from the same edges as ddg_uses, and every frontier append is\nmembership-tested, so a popped pair always has uses. The protection did not\ndisappear -- it moved to SEEDING, which is the earlier and more precise place.\nKept as defensive with a pragma (without it a future unvalidated append gets a\nTypeError instead of the conservative answer) and its comment rewritten,\nbecause the old text asserted something about the present that had stopped\nbeing true.\n\nMEASUREMENT NOW OWED. Every cohort number from 2026-08-03 was taken on the old\nsubstrate and is stale: 16 confirmations, \"section 4 buys nothing\", 264 escape\nsites, 47 distinct callees. Deferring the re-run was correct while INV-rozaj's\nkey fix could not reach those numbers and while this change was still pending;\nthat argument has now expired."  # 9283
- op: discuss  # 3569
  at: '2026-08-08T21:03:20Z'  # 3569
  by: agent  # 3569
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3569
  clock: 5  # 3569
  nonce: '3569'  # 3569
  message: "ROOT_CAUSE IS OBSOLETE; THE TITLE CLAUSE IS NOW VIOLATED BY A DIFFERENT FIELD\nVALUE. Refile, do not close.\n\nThe filed root_cause predates §3a being implemented. §3a exists and the walk\nruns (68 invocations measured). ddg_forward / def_block are no longer blockers.\n\nTHE INCLUSION HALF STILL HOLDS EXACTLY: 0 of 1,352 findings had inclusion\ndecided by the DDG. 68 walks = 20 True / 0 False / 48 None, and every non-True\nflow was still reported, because §3a tests `is True` only.\nCAVEAT ON THAT ZERO: it is near-tautological -- the code path guarantees it. It\nmeasures the implementation, not corpus behaviour. Do not cite it as evidence\nthat the walk is ineffective on real code.\n\nNEW: the violation now runs through `ddg_mixed`, not `ddg`. 526 of 634\nddg_mixed findings (83.0%, 6 repos) are CROSS-FUNCTION, where the walk is\nSTRUCTURALLY INAPPLICABLE (the sink_node == source_fn guard), while the field's\ndocumented meaning is \"the walk ran and did not confirm one\". That is a label\nasserting something that never happened.\n\nLABEL HONESTY WHERE THE WALK DID RUN: 8/8 ddg/precise findings adjudicated from\nsource show a genuine reaching-def chain (6 Go, 2 Python). The precise label is\nearned; the mixed label is not.\n\nTWO CONCRETE REMEDIES:\n 1. A vocabulary value for \"walk not applicable (cross-function)\" -- distinct\n    from \"walk ran, did not confirm\". This is actionable NOW and independent of\n    removal authority.\n 2. §3a removal authority -- which would buy ZERO on this corpus (3a:False =\n    0/68 walks).\n\nINSTRUMENT DEFECT recorded: a probe CRASHED on mitmproxy (wrapper arity, rc=1)\nand its 21-finding stub entered every total. Corrected totals: 1,352 findings,\n68 walks. mitmproxy is NOT a zero-walk repo."  # 3569
