      root_cause: "ADR-0017 section 3a was specified and never implemented: propagate_taint_ddg decided inclusion by call-graph BFS and used the DDG only to select the confidence label. A second, independent blocker: ddg_edge.def_block is a function-local block id compared against a symbol id, so that branch can never fire.\n\nSTALE-IDENTIFIER CORRECTION, 2026-08-09: this field previously cited 'ddg_forward (taint.py:1584-1587)' and 'tainted_at (1651/1658)'. NEITHER IDENTIFIER EXISTS IN taint.py ANY MORE (verified by grep on merged dev), and those line numbers now point at unrelated sanitizer-gate code. A reader following them finds nothing. The mechanism claim is not withdrawn -- the live carrier is dataflow_scope.INCLUSION_DECIDED_BY, which is what production publishes and what this item's clause S2 is about -- but the code coordinates were dead and are removed rather than left to send the next reader on a search."  # 7820
