  message: "ROOT_CAUSE DE-STALED, 2026-08-09 -- code coordinates only, no claim withdrawn.\n\nThe field named two identifiers as the mechanism's carriers: ddg_forward\n(taint.py:1584-1587) and tainted_at (1651/1658). VERIFIED ON MERGED DEV:\n`grep -n 'ddg_forward\\|tainted_at' taint.py` returns NOTHING -- both were\nremoved by later refactors -- and lines 1584-1587 / 1651 / 1658 now sit inside\nunrelated sanitizer-gate code, so the citations actively mislead.\n\nReplaced with the live carrier (dataflow_scope.INCLUSION_DECIDED_BY). The\nstatement, the S2 clause and the violated status are all UNCHANGED; this is a\ndecayed-pointer fix, not a re-measurement, and it is NOT closure evidence for\nanything.\n\nThe 2026-08-08 thread entry remains the current substantive account."  # 2e81
- op: discuss  # 5410
  at: '2026-08-10T10:08:46Z'  # 5410
  by: agent  # 5410
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5410
  clock: 8  # 5410
  nonce: '5410'  # 5410
  message: "SECTION 7B ATTRIBUTION IN MY 2026-08-04 NOTE ABOVE IS RETRACTED, 2026-08-10.\n\nThat entry reads: \"The blocker is that 40.5% of escape sites are not calls at all, so no summary can resolve them; that needs field-sensitivity / alias analysis, which ADR-0017 section 7b excludes. Filed as INV-busis.\" Both halves are refuted on INV-busis's own thread, and its live fields have now been corrected to match:\n\n  (1) 40.5% was computed over the WRONG POPULATION -- all escape sites, including those a CONFIRMING walk passed through and which blocked nothing. The blocked-walk non-call share is 66.7% (48/72 unique pretix sites), 90.6% excluding source_undefined, 75/127 pooled over 4 repos.\n\n  (2) The section 7b attribution is wrong twice over. By SHAPE: container subscript measures 0 in every run and capture-mediated closure -- the only shape section 7b forbids -- has appeared once (3 Go func-literal sites in caddy, 0 in Python). By STRUCTURE, which is the deciding leg: the section 3a arm tests `is True`, so False and None collapse there, and the barrier arm (sole consumer of a False) ran 0 times on every measured repo. No escape reclassification, including section 7a field sensitivity, can move a finding today.\n\nNOTHING ABOUT THIS ITEM'S STATUS CHANGES. Clause S2 stays violated for the reason its own live fields already give: inclusion is decided by call-graph BFS and section 3a is confirm-only. What changes is that this thread no longer names a scope ruling as the terminal cause, sending the next reader to look for an owner decision that was never needed. The live blockers are INV-mumov (50% of call-node escapes), the section 4 summary-catalogue gap (30.8%), and removal authority parked on WI-joluk.\n\nThis entry corrects the record rather than editing the 2026-08-04 note, which stays as filed."  # 5410
